Station: Kor-road, Bori Metropolis.

The interpreted resistivity profile for the four-layer model is 1916, 1252, 1658, and 581 $\Omega \cdot m$. Following the specified curve-type notation, the first triplet (1916, 1252, 1658) follows the $r_1 > r_2 < r_3$ pattern, which is classified as H. The second triplet (1252, 1658, 581) follows the $r_1 < r_2 > r_3$ pattern, which is classified as K. Consequently, the calculated curve type is HK. Please note that the AK-type label provided in the published survey does not match the resistivity values in the interpreted model.

